<title>USA: Dr Pepper Bottling to acquire Seven-Up Bottling.</title>
<headline>Dr Pepper Bottling to acquire Seven-Up Bottling.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dr. Pepper Bottling Co of Texas said Monday it had entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Seven-Up/RC Bottling Co of Southern California Inc for $12.00 a share.</p>
<p>The company said DPB Acquisition Corp, a wholly-owned subsidiary that it had recently created, will make a cash tender offer for Seven-Up/RC Botting.</p>
<p>Once the tender was completed, DPB will merge into the bottling company, it said.</p>
<p>Dr Pepper Bottling Co of Texas is an independent franchise bottler of &quot;Dr Pepper&quot; brand soda products.</p>
</text>
